WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.300
Meet Eagle, the spacecraft that landed on the Moon!

00:03.600 --> 00:10.700
In 1969, Neil Armstrong and Buzz Aldrin reached the Moon in a small spacecraft named Eagle.

00:11.000 --> 00:13.300
They landed in the Sea of Tranquility.

00:13.600 --> 00:18.700
The mission was a success! But did you know Eagle had two parts?

00:19.200 --> 00:24.000
The top part was the astronauts’ cabin—it had an engine to fly back to space.

00:24.500 --> 00:28.700
The bottom part had four legs that helped it land gently.

00:29.300 --> 00:33.800
The astronauts walked on the Moon, collected rocks, and took photographs.

00:34.300 --> 00:38.600
After more than 21 hours, it was time to depart!

00:38.600 --> 00:43.700
The top part blasted off to reunite with Columbia, where Michael Collins was waiting.

00:44.200 --> 00:50.600
And the bottom part stayed on the Moon—and it’s still there after 57 years!
